### 9. **Blended Linking Strategy (Clear Implementation)**

**CRITICAL: Link Implementation Requirements - Execute Precisely:**

**Total Link Count (Length-Scaled):**
- 6–25 total links (internal + external combined), scaled by article length:
  - **< 1,800 words** → 6–10 total links
  - **1,800–3,200 words** → 10–16 total links
  - **> 3,200 words** → 16–25 total links

**Link Priority & Distribution:**
-   [ ] **Internal Links First** - When internal URLs provided: target 60–80% internal links of total count
-   [ ] **External Links MANDATORY** - ALWAYS include minimum 4-6 relevant external sources from Phase 2 research (20–40% of total). Use ONLY URLs from your "EXTERNAL LINK INVENTORY" that you verified were in actual web search results. DO NOT generate or create new URLs.
-   [ ] **External Only Fallback** - If no internal URLs provided, fulfill entire count with high-quality external links from verified search results only

**Placement Rules:**
-   [ ] **DISTRIBUTE EVENLY** - Place 1–2 links per major section throughout article, including introduction when contextually relevant
-   [ ] **CONTEXTUAL RELEVANCE** - Each link must directly support, extend, or exemplify the specific point in that paragraph
-   [ ] **AVOID CLUSTERING** - Do not cluster multiple links in one area; spread them naturally throughout content
-   [ ] **INTERNAL LINKS FORMATTING** - Internal links must NOT have target="_blank" attribute. Format: <a href="URL">text</a>. Only external links get target="_blank".

**Link Quality Standards:**
-   [ ] **VERIFIED URLS ONLY** - Use ONLY URLs from your Phase 2 search results inventory. Never generate, construct, or assume URLs.
-   [ ] **ANCHOR TEXT** - Use natural, contextual anchor text that flows with the sentence (2-5 words). Avoid repetitive patterns like "Topic in Location". Examples: "similar techniques", "related strategies", "other resources"
-   [ ] **LINK FORMAT** - Internal links: <a href="URL">text</a> (no target, no rel). External links: <a target="_blank" href="URL">text</a>
-   [ ] **CRITICAL - NO REL ATTRIBUTE**: NEVER add rel="nofollow" or rel="noreferrer" to links. Leave rel attribute COMPLETELY OMITTED. Only use target="_blank" for external links, nothing else.
-   [ ] **EDITORIAL VALUE** - Link must genuinely enhance reader understanding or provide valuable additional information
-   [ ] **NO HOMEPAGE LINKS** - Link to specific, relevant pages, not general homepages
-   [ ] **CANONICAL URLS** - Prefer authoritative, canonical sources over duplicates from search results
-   [ ] **NATURAL FLOW** - Anchor text should read naturally when spoken aloud as part of the full sentence
-   [ ] **SEARCH RESULT VERIFICATION** - Double-check each external URL was actually in your web search results before adding it
-   [ ] **RELEVANCE OVER QUANTITY** - If the topic or article length does not allow natural placement of the full scaled link count, prioritize relevance and editorial value over hitting the number. A shorter article with 6 genuinely useful links is better than one with 16 forced ones

**LINKING EXECUTION:**
